#. Tag: title
#: qt.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Qt; and Licensing questions"
msgstr "Perguntas acerca da &Qt; e das licenzas"

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is &Qt;, by the way?"
msgstr "Xa postos, que é &Qt;?"

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:11
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "&Qt; is a C++-based class library to build user interfaces. It also "
#| "includes many utility classes like string classes and classes to handle "
#| "input and output. It provides most of the widgets you will see in a &kde; "
#| "application: menus, buttons, sliders, &etc;. &Qt; is a cross-platform "
#| "library that allows you to write code that will compile on &UNIX; systems "
#| "as well as &Windows; and embedded devices. You can learn more about &Qt; "
#| "at <ulink url=\"http://www.trolltech.com\">http://www.trolltech.com</"
#| "ulink>."
msgid ""
"&Qt; is a C++-based class library to build user interfaces. It also includes "
"many utility classes like string classes and classes to handle input and "
"output. It provides most of the widgets you will see in a &kde; application: "
"menus, buttons, sliders, &etc;. &Qt; is a cross-platform library that allows "
"you to write code that will compile on &UNIX; systems as well as &Windows; "
"and embedded devices. You can learn more about &Qt; at <ulink url=\"http://"
"www.qtsoftware.com\">http://www.qtsoftware.com</ulink>."
msgstr ""
"&Qt; é unha biblioteca baseada en C++ de clases para construir interfaces de "
"usuario. Tamén inclúe moitas clases de utilidade como clases para cadeas e "
"para xestionar a entrada e a saída. Fornece a maioría dos widgets que verá "
"nun programa de &kde;: menús, botóns, barras deslizantes, &etc;. &Qt; é unha "
"biblioteca multiplataforma que lle permite escreber código que compile nos "
"sistemas &UNIX; e nos &Windows; e en sistemas empotrados. Pode aprender máis "
"acerca de &Qt; en <ulink url=\"http://www.trolltech.com\">http://www."
"trolltech.com</ulink>."

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why does &kde; use &Qt;?"
msgstr "Porque emprega &kde; as &Qt;?"

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&Qt; is a very sophisticated toolkit that provides everything that is needed "
"to build a modern user interface. &Qt; is written in C++, thus allowing "
"object-oriented development which ensures efficiency and code reuse in a "
"project the size and scope of &kde;. In our opinion there is no better "
"toolkit available for &UNIX; systems and that it would have been a grave "
"mistake to try to build &kde; on anything but the best."
msgstr ""
"&Qt; é un toolkit moi sofisticado que fornece todo o que é preciso para "
"construir unha interface de usuario moderna. &Qt; está escrita en C++, o que "
"permite facer desenvolvimento orientado a obxectos, garantindo a eficiencia "
"e a reutilización de código nun proxecto do tamaño e extensión de &kde;. Na "
"nosa opinión non hai un toolkit mellor disponíbel para os sistemas &UNIX;, e "
"tería sido un grave erro tentar construir &kde; en calquera cousa que non "
"fose a mellor."

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:39
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Why does &kde; not use gtk, xforms, xlib, whatever?"
msgid "Why does &kde; not use GTK, XForms, Xlib, whatever?"
msgstr "Por que non emprega &kde; a gtk, xforms, xlib ou outra?"

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a number of toolkits available. To provide a consistent user "
"interface and to keep used resources such as memory to a minimum, &kde; can "
"use only one of them. &Qt; was selected for the reasons mentioned above."
msgstr ""
"Hai varios toolkits disponíbeis. Para fornecer unha interface de usuario "
"consistente e manter os recursos empregados, como memoria, no mínimo, &kde; "
"so debe empregar un deles. &Qt; foi escollida polos motivos antes "
"mencionados."

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid "But &Qt; isn't free, is it?"
msgstr "Pero &Qt; non é libre, non si?"

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:54
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "It is! As of September 4, 2000, version 2.2 of the &Qt; libraries were "
#| "licensed under the <acronym>GPL</acronym>, thereby fulfiling all aspects "
#| "of <quote>free software</quote>."
msgid ""
"It is! As of September 4, 2000, version 2.2 of the &Qt; libraries were "
"licensed under the <acronym>GPL</acronym>, thereby fulfiling all aspects of "
"<quote>free software</quote>. Since version 4.5.0 Qt is also available under "
"the <acronym>LGPL</acronym>."
msgstr ""
"Claro que o é! O día 4 de setembro de 200, a versión 2.2 das bibliotecas "
"&Qt; foron licenciadas sob a <acronym>GPL</acronym>, satisfacendo deste "
"xeito todos os requerimentos do <quote>software libre</quote>."

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I write commercial software for &kde;?"
msgstr "Podo escreber software comercial para &kde;?"

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:66
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "You can use the &kde; libraries to write <quote>commercial and closed "
#| "source</quote> as well as <quote>commercial and open source</quote> "
#| "software. If you write open source software you can use the &Qt; free "
#| "edition. But if you write closed source software you may not use the &Qt; "
#| "free edition; you need to obtain the &Qt; professional edition from Troll "
#| "Tech."
msgid ""
"You can use the &kde; libraries to write <quote>commercial and closed "
"source</quote> as well as <quote>commercial and open source</quote> "
"software. If you want to write open source software you can use the &Qt; "
"free edition. But if you intend to write closed source software you may not "
"use the &Qt; free edition; you need to obtain the &Qt; professional edition "
"from Qt Software."
msgstr ""
"Pode empregar as bibliotecas de &kde; para escreber software "
"<quote>comercial e privativo</quote> así como <quote>comercial e libre</"
"quote>. Se escrebe sóftware open source pode empregar as &Qt; free edition. "
"Pero se escrebe software privativo non pode empregar as &Qt; free edition, "
"deberá obter a &Qt; professional edition de Troll Tech."

#. Tag: para
#: qt.docbook:71
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "If you want more information, please contact <ulink url=\"http://www."
#| "trolltech.com\">Troll Tech</ulink> directly."
msgid ""
"If you want more information, please contact <ulink url=\"http://www."
"qtsoftware.com\">Qt Software</ulink> directly."
msgstr ""
"Se desexa máis información, contacte con <ulink url=\"http://www.trolltech."
"com\">Troll Tech</ulink> directamente."
